From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] No system CPU probe on Windows

CpuProbe::Create returns no probe on Windows, as on platforms without
one; every caller already handles that. The probe's PDH queries
delay-load pdh.dll on a browser thread pool worker as soon as the
performance manager starts, and in the Rockstar launcher's Open that
load failed when the JIT pool was full and Chromium ended the browser
(PLA-394). Apply after the pinned CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-18-cef-late-children.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 components/system_cpu/cpu_probe.cc |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/system_cpu/cpu_probe.cc b/components/system_cpu/cpu_probe.cc
index 4c9bdb9cc8..3801d75748 100644
--- a/components/system_cpu/cpu_probe.cc
+++ b/components/system_cpu/cpu_probe.cc
@@ -27,7 +27,9 @@ std::unique_ptr<CpuProbe> CpuProbe::Create() {
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
   return CpuProbeLinux::Create();
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
-  return CpuProbeWin::Create();
+  // No system CPU probe on Windows: its PDH queries load pdh.dll, and the
+  // browser ends itself when that delay-load fails.
+  return nullptr;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
   return CpuProbeMac::Create();
 #else
